# Test vectors are binary. A constant-colour Y4M has no NUL bytes, so git's
# heuristic would call it text and a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf would
# rewrite its line endings and corrupt it.
*.pwv1 binary
*.y4m binary

# Shaders keep LF on every checkout: a test cuts a function out of idwt.wgsl
# by its text, and the shaders are compiled from these files as they are.
*.wgsl text eol=lf

# The C header is generated, and tests/header.rs compares it with cbindgen's
# output byte for byte.
*.h text eol=lf

# The README's picture of the quality is a frame of a game, Pearl Abyss's and
